        <om-2:longcomment xml:lang="en">The volt is a unit of electric potential defined as watt divided by ampere = joule divided by coulomb = newton times metre divided by ampere times second = kilogram times square metre divided by ampere times second to the power 3. The volt is a derived unit in the International System of Units.</om-2:longcomment>
